### MCP Gateway on SAP Integration Suite — principal propagation to an on-prem SAP backend
### Two things to test:
###   A) The quick foil — call the SAP backend directly with HTTP Basic Authentication
###      (verifies the service + a technical user; note it always runs as that one user).
###   B) The goal — call the MCP Gateway with the SAP IAS bearer token obtained via Entra ID.
###      Once principal propagation is wired (Part B of the guide), the backend runs the call
###      as the REAL end user. Same IAS token flow as: mcp-gateway-entra-id-copilot-studio.md
###
### Run with the VS Code REST Client extension.
### Fill in the placeholders (<...>) with your own values. Never commit real
### credentials or IAS tokens.

########################################################################
### A) Stage 0/2 — call the SAP backend (HE4, client 400) directly with Basic Auth
########################################################################

@backend = https://<your-sap-backend-host>:44301/sap/opu/odata/sap/API_BUSINESS_PARTNER
@backendUser = <technical ABAP user>
@backendPass = <that user's password>

### A1. List the first 5 business partners
# The REST Client encodes "user:pass" after "Basic " for you.
# @name backendBP
GET {{backend}}/A_BusinessPartner?$top=5&$format=json&sap-client=400
Authorization: Basic {{backendUser}}:{{backendPass}}
Accept: application/json

### A2. Get a single business partner by key (replace with a real BP number from A1)
# @name backendBPByKey
GET {{backend}}/A_BusinessPartner('1000000')?$format=json&sap-client=400
Authorization: Basic {{backendUser}}:{{backendPass}}
Accept: application/json

########################################################################
### B0) Obtain a SAP IAS access token (for the MCP Gateway calls below)
###     In the video this comes from the Entra ID -> IAS browser flow (Copilot Studio).
###     For a scripted check you can use the IAS OIDC endpoints directly.
########################################################################

@ias = https://<your-ias-tenant>.trial-accounts.ondemand.com

### B0a. Inspect the IAS OpenID configuration (issuer, jwks_uri, token_endpoint)
###       These values also feed the SAP MCP external-auth policy.
# @name iasWellKnown
GET {{ias}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
Accept: application/json

### B0b. (Optional) Resource-owner password grant against IAS, IF password auth is enabled
###       for the application. Otherwise get the token via the browser flow as in Video 3.
@iasClientId = <IAS application client_id>
@iasClientSecret = <IAS application client_secret>
@iasUser = <IAS/Entra login email, e.g. user@contoso.onmicrosoft.com>
@iasUserPass = <that user's password>
# @name iasToken
POST {{ias}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id={{iasClientId}}&client_secret={{iasClientSecret}}&username={{iasUser}}&password={{iasUserPass}}&scope=openid

########################################################################
### B) Stage 2/4 — call the MCP Gateway with the SAP IAS bearer token (via Entra ID)
###    Obtain the IAS access_token exactly as in the previous video:
###    mcp-gateway-entra-id-copilot-studio.md
###    With principal propagation configured, the backend runs as the signed-in user.
########################################################################

# Find this on the Integration Suite tenant (API Management), NOT the CF API host.
@MCP-Server-URL = <your MCP Server URL, e.g. https://<tenant>.integrationsuite.../business-partner>
# Use the token from B0b, or paste one obtained from the Copilot Studio / browser flow:
@iasToken = {{iasToken.response.body.access_token}}

### B1. Initialize the MCP session
# @name init
POST {{MCP-Server-URL}}
Authorization: Bearer {{iasToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-06-18",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "vscode-rest", "version": "1.0" }
  }
}

### B2. List the exposed MCP tools (reuses the Mcp-Session-Id from init)
# @name toolsList
POST {{MCP-Server-URL}}
Authorization: Bearer {{iasToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Mcp-Session-Id: {{init.response.headers.mcp-session-id}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list"
}

### B3. Call the getBusinessPartners tool (runs as the real user once PP is wired)
# @name callTool
POST {{MCP-Server-URL}}
Authorization: Bearer {{iasToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Mcp-Session-Id: {{init.response.headers.mcp-session-id}}

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "getBusinessPartners",
    "arguments": { "$top": 5, "$format": "json" }
  }
}
